<title>MEXICO: Mexico sugar crop seen ending near to 95-96 record.</title>
<headline>Mexico sugar crop seen ending near to 95-96 record.</headline>
<byline>Chris Aspin</byline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's sugar harvest, now winding down after topping the 4 million tonne mark in mid-May, is seen coming close but not necessarily touching a new record this 1996-1997 cycle, sugar sources said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The political will is there to reach a record, the government wants this to happen,&quot; said one industrialist. &quot;It all depends on the rains and if they start to hamper scheduled milling in important states, especially Veracruz,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
